    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Proclaimed on 1 December 1918 as the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>, it united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, Montenegro and former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> lands.</li><li>Conflict between Serbian centralism and Croatian autonomy led to the royal dictatorship of 1929 and the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> invasion of April 1941 destroyed the kingdom in eleven days and partitioned it among its enemies.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>King Alexander’s assassination in Marseille in 1934 was filmed by newsreel cameramen, making it one of the first political assassinations recorded on film.</p></aside>
    </section>

